--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT THE WEB SOURCE IS (parity target)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SlideRenderer.tsx is a composition/DISPATCH surface, not a data view. It receives one already-resolved
`YearReview`, a `SlideDefinition` (`type` + Tailwind gradient `bg` + optional `field`), and a `slideIndex`;
it `AnimatePresence mode="wait"`-wraps a `bg-gradient-to-br ${slide.bg}` `motion.div` keyed by the index
(enter x:+50/opacity-in, exit x:-50/opacity-out, 0.35s easeInOut) and `switch (slide.type)`-dispatches to
one of ten child slide components. The ONLY t() calls the renderer itself owns are the two drive-highlight
labels it forwards:
    t('yearReview.longestDrive','Longest Drive')   (emoji 🏔️, drive = data.longest_drive)
    t('yearReview.mostEfficient','Most Efficient Drive') (emoji 🌿, drive = data.most_efficient_drive)
Everything else it forwards verbatim (`<ChildSlide data={data} />`). The child slides (TitleSlide,
StatHeroSlide, …) are SEPARATE P4 prompts (Out of Scope here).

