Architecture decision (matches the established `DashboardGrid<WidgetBody>` dispatcher in this codebase):
SlideRenderer is generic over the slide body; the parent injects the REAL child surfaces (each its own P4
prompt). This file therefore does NOT hard-depend on the sibling slide view types — three of them
(DriveHighlightSlide, ChargingBreakdownSlide, ComparisonsSlide) are not yet ported, and the generic seam
keeps SlideRenderer compiling and shippable today. A built-in, data-bound default body composes a complete
recap so every P4 state renders in isolation (previews/tests) and in production until the child surfaces are
wired. Slide bodies sit on a fixed dark ×900 gradient, so their ink is fixed-light (parity with the web
`text-white` slides), while the load/empty/error chrome uses the adaptive Color.TS tokens.

Parity reproduced exactly from the web source:
  • The 2 owned i18n keys (yearReview.longestDrive / yearReview.mostEfficient) with the exact English values.
  • The drive-highlight selection it owns: field==="longest" -> longest_drive + 🏔️; else -> most_efficient_drive
    + 🌿 (pinned by tests; verified longest 612 km / 6h 14m / 168 Wh/km, efficient 84 km / 1h 36m / 121 Wh/km).
  • The gradient: every web SLIDE_DEFS `bg` token resolves against the Tailwind ×900 palette (audit test
    asserts no deck token falls back); bg-gradient-to-br top-leading->bottom-trailing.
  • The keyed enter/exit transition (x:+50 in / x:-50 out + opacity, easeInOut), Reduce-Motion -> crossfade.
  • The web `default: return null` arm -> SlideHero.none (gradient only).
States (P4): loading (skeleton), empty (ContentUnavailableView), error (retry), stale + offline (cached deck +
freshness chip + banner), content. All implemented + each has a #if DEBUG preview + unit-tested phase logic.

i18n: the surface holds no bare English literals (all via SlideRendererStrings). The 2 source keys are present
with their exact web values; native chrome/default-composition strings are namespaced slideRenderer.* so they
never collide with the sibling slide surfaces' own per-surface tables.

